    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d258">

                <pb facs="0369" n="301" xml:id="pg301"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">763.72112/1381</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        President Wilson
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-07-27">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 27, 1915</hi>.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. President</hi>: I enclose a copy of the
                    English note<anchor n="80" xml:id="d258-f1"/> we have received in reply to ours
                    of March 30th. It was intended to have this note published simultaneously in
                    England and the United States Wednesday morning, but last night I received a
                    telegram from Mr. Page,<anchor n="81" xml:id="d258-f2"/> saying that Sir Edward
                    Grey would have ready within a week another note dealing with the practical
                    questions relating to shipping, and he therefore requested that publication be
                    delayed until the latter note had been delivered.</p>
                <p>Faithfully yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
